The five non-blocking points are clean-ups for the author, and none affects safety. The most useful are R1, wrapping a raw `waitid` error in a SmokeError, and R3, making the failure-case test check the exact error for each case.

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- Two things in the code keep this safe on their own. First, the leader stays unreaped, so its PID and process group can't be reused while it is signalled. Second, only a "no such process" error (ESRCH) from the post-reap check counts as proof the group is gone. Even if the zombie confirmation were somehow wrong, any member still alive would make that final check fail.
- In `run_bounded`, the `finally` block retries cleanup only while `child.returncode is None`. Because of that guard, the "no nonzero signal after reaping" rule also holds when `_finish_child` fails partway through, not just in `_finish_child` itself.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`
